<body>
<header><div class="brand"><div class="logo">⌂</div><div><b>HIPSTEEL</b><small>ROOF TRUSS DESIGNER</small></div></div><div class="topright"><span class="pill"><i class="statusdot"></i>Local calculations</span><span class="pill">NSCP 2015 · LRFD study</span></div></header>
<main>
<div class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Concept design workspace</div><h1>Hip roof truss optimizer</h1><p>Explore roof geometry, load effects and preliminary steel sizing in one place.</p></div><div class="actions"><button class="btn" id="reset">Reset inputs</button><button class="btn primary" id="export">Export summary</button></div></div>
<div class="notice"><b>Engineering review required.</b> This is an educational, preliminary sizing aid—not a code-certified design. It implements simplified 2D axial truss analysis and selected LRFD combinations only. Verify NSCP 2015 loads, wind/seismic, stability, member slenderness, connections, bracing, serviceability, load paths and all applicable provisions with a Philippine-licensed structural engineer before construction.</div>
<div class="tabs"><button class="tab active" data-page="design">Design studio</button><button class="tab" data-page="calculations">Calculations</button><button class="tab" data-page="optimization">Optimization</button><button class="tab" data-page="notes">Assumptions & references</button></div>
<section class="tabpage active" id="design">
<div class="layout">
<aside class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>Project inputs</h2><small>SI units</small></div><div class="pad">
<div class="sectionlabel">Roof geometry</div>
<div class="field"><label for="length">Building length</label><div class="control"><input id="length" type="number" min="2" step=".1" value="12"><span class="unit">m</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="width">Building width / span</label><div class="control"><input id="width" type="number" min="2" step=".1" value="8"><span class="unit">m</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="pitch">Roof pitch</label><div class="control"><input id="pitch" type="number" min="5" max="60" step="1" value="25"><span class="unit">°</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="spacing">Truss spacing</label><div class="control"><input id="spacing" type="number" min=".3" step=".1" value="1.2"><span class="unit">m</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="panels">Truss panels</label><div class="control"><select id="panels"><option>4</option><option selected>6</option><option>8</option><option>10</option><option>12</option></select></div></div>
<div class="sectionlabel">Loads (service)</div>
<div class="field"><label for="dead">Roof dead load</label><div class="control"><input id="dead" type="number" min="0" step=".05" value=".75"><span class="unit">kPa</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="rooflive">Roof live load, Lr</label><div class="control"><input id="rooflive" type="number" min="0" step=".05" value=".96"><span class="unit">kPa</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="wind">Net uplift wind*</label><div class="control"><input id="wind" type="number" min="0" step=".05" value=".8"><span class="unit">kPa</span></div></div>
<div class="hint">*Simplified user-entered net pressure used as uniform uplift sensitivity only. Not a NSCP wind calculation.</div>
<div class="sectionlabel">Steel & design</div>
<div class="field"><label for="fy">Yield strength, Fy</label><div class="control"><input id="fy" type="number" min="100" step="5" value="250"><span class="unit">MPa</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="E">Elastic modulus, E</label><div class="control"><input id="E" type="number" min="100000" step="1000" value="200000"><span class="unit">MPa</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="r">Assumed radius, r</label><div class="control"><input id="r" type="number" min="5" step="1" value="20"><span class="unit">mm</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="K">Effective length factor, K</label><div class="control"><input id="K" type="number" min=".5" max="2" step=".05" value="1"><span class="unit">—</span></div></div>
<div class="hint">Single uniform trial area; idealized pin joints and braced member lengths. Configure appropriate section properties in real design.</div>
</div></aside>
<div class="content">
<div class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>3D roof assembly</h2><small id="geomSummary">Hip roof · interactive schematic</small></div><div class="visual"><canvas id="scene"></canvas><div class="viewtools"><button class="iconbtn" id="rotate">↻ Rotate</button><button class="iconbtn" id="zoom">＋ Zoom</button><button class="iconbtn" id="fit">Fit view</button></div><div class="viewlabel">SCHEMATIC GEOMETRY · NOT FOR FABRICATION</div><div class="legend"><span><i style="background:#56e0c2"></i>Top chords</span><span><i style="background:#71b8ff"></i>Webs / ties</span></div></div></div>
<div class="metrics">
<div class="metric"><span>PRELIMINARY STATUS</span><strong id="status" class="rating">—</strong><small id="statusSub">Solving model</small></div>
<div class="metric"><span>OPTIMIZATION RATING</span><strong id="rating" class="rating">—</strong><small id="ratingSub">steel mass vs. feasible trial</small></div>
<div class="metric"><span>EST. STEEL MASS</span><strong id="mass">—</strong><small>trusses + main truss members</small></div>
<div class="metric"><span>GOVERNING UTILIZATION</span><strong id="util">—</strong><small id="gov">—</small></div>
</div>
<div class="lower"><div class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>Member sizing summary</h2><small id="sizeSummary">uniform trial section</small></div><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>MEMBER GROUP</th><th>MAX AXIAL</th><th>GOVERNING CASE</th><th>UTIL.</th><th>CHECK</th></tr></thead><tbody id="memberRows"></tbody></table></div></div><div class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>Load cases</h2><small>LRFD combinations</small></div><div class="pad"><div class="chips"><span class="chip">1.4D</span><span class="chip">1.2D + 1.6Lr</span><span class="chip">1.2D + 1.0W + 0.5Lr</span><span class="chip">0.9D + 1.0W</span></div><p class="explain">Screening combinations based on NSCP 2015 strength-design concepts. The app applies vertical pressure to a representative 2D common truss; roof zones, pattern loading, drift, internal pressure, seismic, rain and load reversals require project-specific analysis.</p></div></div></div>
</div></div></section>
<section class="tabpage" id="calculations"><div class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>Analysis and design calculations</h2><small>live update</small></div><div class="pad" id="calcContent"></div></div></section>
<section class="tabpage" id="optimization"><div class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>Steel-use optimization</h2><small>uniform area catalog search</small></div><div class="pad" id="optContent"></div></div></section>
<section class="tabpage" id="notes"><div class="card"><div class="cardhead"><h2>Model scope, assumptions & references</h2></div><div class="pad">
<p class="explain">This single-file tool is a preliminary concept explorer, not an implementation of all NSCP 2015 requirements. It models one common roof truss as a planar pin-jointed truss, solves linear elastic axial response, and searches an illustrative area/radius catalog. Hip-end framing is shown in the 3D schematic; its jack, hip and valley members are not analyzed by the planar solver. The displayed whole-roof mass extrapolates one uniform truss at the selected spacing and is a rough material indicator.</p>
<div class="sectionlabel">Model assumptions</div><ul class="explain"><li>Roof dimensions define a symmetric hip roof; common truss analyzed across the full width. End hip framing and 3D diaphragm action are not included in force analysis.</li><li>Uniform dead, roof live and user-entered net uplift pressures are applied to top-chord panel points using tributary area. Wind pressure is not generated from site parameters.</li><li>Linear first-order stiffness solution; pin joints; no member self-weight iteration, second-order effects, imperfections, flexure, local buckling, torsional/flexural-torsional buckling or connection eccentricity.</li><li>Illustrative compression screening uses Euler elastic buckling with the inelastic column curve and the user-entered K, r, Fy, E; it does not replace complete NSCP/AISC section checks. Tension screens gross yielding only.</li><li>Cost, fabrication, availability, connection design, roof cladding, purlins, bracing, supports and foundation are excluded from optimization rating.</li></ul>
<div class="sectionlabel">References</div><p class="explain">National Structural Code of the Philippines (NSCP), Volume 1, 7th Edition (2015), Chapters 2 and 5. Obtain and apply the licensed code text and current local authority requirements. Steel-member screening is informed by the AISC LRFD column curve but is not a claim of full NSCP/AISC compliance.</p><div class="chips"><a class="chip" href="https://aseponline.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Association of Structural Engineers of the Philippines</a><a class="chip" href="https://www.aisc.org/aisc/publications/current-standards/aisc-360/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AISC 360 standards overview</a></div>
<div class="notice" style="margin-top:16px"><b>Do not use this output for construction, permitting or procurement.</b> An engineer must independently establish design criteria and verify every applicable limit state.</div>
</div></div></section>
<div class="foot">HIPSTEEL · Offline, self-contained HTML · Preliminary engineering study only · Inputs remain in your browser and are not transmitted.</div>
<script>
(function(){
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id), ids=['length','width','pitch','spacing','panels','dead','rooflive','wind','fy','E','r','K'];let state={rot:.45,zoom:1,last:null};
const catalog=[500,650,800,1000,1250,1500,1800,2200,2700,3300,4000,5000,6500,8000,10000,12500,16000,20000,25000,32000,40000,50000];
function solve(A,b){let n=b.length,m=A.map((r,i)=>r.slice().concat(b[i]));for(let k=0;k<n;k++){let p=k;for(let i=k+1;i<n;i++)if(Math.abs(m[i][k])>Math.abs(m[p][k]))p=i;if(Math.abs(m[p][k])<1e-10)throw Error('Unstable or singular truss. Change panel count or geometry.');[m[k],m[p]]=[m[p],m[k]];let d=m[k][k];for(let j=k;j<=n;j++)m[k][j]/=d;for(let i=0;i<n;i++)if(i!==k){let f=m[i][k];for(let j=k;j<=n;j++)m[i][j]-=f*m[k][j]}}return m.map(r=>r[n])}
function model(){
let v=Object.fromEntries(ids.map(x=>[x,+$(x).value]));v.panels=+v.panels;
if(Object.values(v).some(x=>!Number.isFinite(x)||x<=0)||v.width<2||v.length<2)throw Error('All inputs must be positive numbers.');
let N=v.panels, half=N, nodes=[],mem=[];
for(let i=0;i<=N;i++){let x=v.width*i/N;nodes.push([x,0]);}
for(let i=0;i<=N;i++){let x=v.width*i/N,y=Math.min(x,v.width-x)*Math.tan(v.pitch*Math.PI/180);nodes.push([x,y]);}
const bot=i=>i,top=i=>N+1+i;
for(let i=0;i<N;i++){mem.push({a:top(i),b:top(i+1),type:'Top chord'});mem.push({a:bot(i),b:bot(i+1),type:'Bottom chord'});}
for(let i=0;i<=N;i++)mem.push({a:bot(i),b:top(i),type:'Web'});
for(let i=0;i<N;i++)mem.push({a:top(i),b:bot(i+1),type:'Web'});
// remove duplicate crossing diagonals? Warren alternating instead
mem=mem.filter((m,i)=>true);
let dof=nodes.length*2,Kmat=Array.from({length:dof},()=>Array(dof).fill(0)),E=v.E*1e6,Aref=1e-3;
mem.forEach(m=>{let [x1,y1]=nodes[m.a],[x2,y2]=nodes[m.b],dx=x2-x1,dy=y2-y1,L=Math.hypot(dx,dy),c=dx/L,s=dy/L,k=E*Aref/L,ix=[2*m.a,2*m.a+1,2*m.b,2*m.b+1],q=[[c*c,c*s,-c*c,-c*s],[c*s,s*s,-c*s,-s*s],[-c*c,-c*s,c*c,c*s],[-c*s,-s*s,c*s,s*s]];m.L=L;m.c=c;m.s=s;for(let i=0;i<4;i++)for(let j=0;j<4;j++)Kmat[ix[i]][ix[j]]+=k*q[i][j];});
let fixed=new Set([0,1,2*N]), free=Array.from({length:dof},(_,i)=>i).filter(i=>!fixed.has(i));
let qN=N+1, trib=v.width/N, loads={D:Array(dof).fill(0),Lr:Array(dof).fill(0),W:Array(dof).fill(0)};
for(let i=0;i<=N;i++){let seg=(i===0||i===N)?trib/2:trib, area=seg*v.spacing;loads.D[2*top(i)+1]=-v.dead*area*1000;loads.Lr[2*top(i)+1]=-v.rooflive*area*1000;loads.W[2*top(i)+1]=v.wind*area*1000;}
let combos=[{name:'1.4D',f:{D:1.4}},{name:'1.2D + 1.6Lr',f:{D:1.2,Lr:1.6}},{name:'1.2D + 1.0W + 0.5Lr',f:{D:1.2,W:1,Lr:.5}},{name:'0.9D + 1.0W',f:{D:.9,W:1}}];
let forceCombos=[];
for(let combo of combos){let F=Array(dof).fill(0);for(let key in combo.f)F=F.map((a,i)=>a+loads[key][i]*combo.f[key]);let u=solve(free.map(i=>free.map(j=>Kmat[i][j])),free.map(i=>F[i]));let disp=Array(dof).fill(0);free.forEach((id,i)=>disp[id]=u[i]);let forces=mem.map(m=>{let d1=disp[2*m.a],d2=disp[2*m.a+1],d3=disp[2*m.b],d4=disp[2*m.b+1];return E*Aref/m.L*((d3-d1)*m.c+(d4-d2)*m.s)});forceCombos.push({name:combo.name,forces,disp});}
let grouped=['Top chord','Bottom chord','Web'].map(type=>{let ix=mem.map((m,i)=>m.type===type?i:-1).filter(i=>i>=0),max=0,which='',member=null;for(let c of forceCombos)for(let i of ix)if(Math.abs(c.forces[i])>max){max=Math.abs(c.forces[i]);which=c.name;member=mem[i]}return{type,force:max,case:which,member}});
let fy=v.fy*1e6,phi=.9;
function capacity(area,m){let tension=phi*fy*area*1e-6;let Fe=Math.PI**2*(v.E*1e6)/(v.K*m.L*1000/(v.r/1000))**2/1e6;let ratio=fy/(Fe*1e6),Fcr=(ratio<=2.25?Math.pow(.658,ratio)*fy:.877*Fe*1e6);return Math.min(tension,phi*Fcr*area);}
function assess(area){let max=0,grp=[];for(let g of grouped){let cap=capacity(area,g.member),u=g.force/cap;grp.push({...g,cap,util:u});max=Math.max(max,u);}return{max,grp};}
let chosen=catalog.find(a=>assess(a/1e6).max<=1)||catalog.at(-1),aM=chosen/1e6,ass=assess(aM),feasible=ass.max<=1;
let lengthSum=mem.reduce((s,m)=>s+m.L,0),massOne=aM*7850*lengthSum,number=Math.ceil(v.length/v.spacing)+1,totalMass=massOne*number;
let minFeas=catalog.find(a=>assess(a/1e6).max<=1)||catalog.at(-1),ratio=ass.max,eff=Math.max(0,Math.min(100,100-(chosen-minFeas)/chosen*100));
return{v,nodes,mem,combos:forceCombos,grouped:ass.grp,area:chosen,areaM:aM,massOne,totalMass,number,util:ratio,feasible,eff,loadTotals:Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(loads).map(k=>[k,loads[k].reduce((s,x)=>s+x,0)])),lengthSum};
}
function run(){try{let d=model();state.last=d;render(d);draw(d)}catch(err){$('status').textContent='CHECK INPUTS';$('statusSub').textContent=err.message;$('memberRows').innerHTML='<tr><td colspan="5">'+err.message+'</td></tr>';}}
function render(d){let fmt=(x,n=2)=>Number(x).toLocaleString(undefined,{maximumFractionDigits:n});$('status').textContent=d.feasible?'PRELIM PASS':'NOT SIZED';$('status').style.color=d.feasible?'var(--green)':'var(--red)';$('statusSub').textContent=d.feasible?'screening checks within trial capacity':'catalog limit reached';$('rating').textContent=d.eff>=90?'A':d.eff>=75?'B':d.eff>=55?'C':'D';$('ratingSub').textContent=fmt(d.area)+' mm² uniform area · '+fmt(d.eff,0)+'% catalog fit';$('mass').textContent=fmt(d.totalMass/1000,2)+' t';$('mass').style.fontSize='19px';$('util').textContent=fmt(d.util*100,0)+'%';$('gov').textContent=d.grouped.slice().sort((a,b)=>b.util-a.util)[0].type+' · '+d.grouped.slice().sort((a,b)=>b.util-a.util)[0].case;$('sizeSummary').textContent=fmt(d.area)+' mm² · '+d.number+' trusses';$('geomSummary').textContent=fmt(d.v.length,1)+' × '+fmt(d.v.width,1)+' m · '+d.v.pitch+'° pitch · hip ends schematic';
$('memberRows').innerHTML=d.grouped.map(g=>'<tr><td>'+g.type+'</td><td>'+fmt(g.force/1000,1)+' kN</td><td>'+g.case+'</td><td>'+fmt(g.util*100,0)+'%</td><td><span class="badge '+(g.util<=1?'pass':'fail')+'">'+(g.util<=1?'SCREEN PASS':'OVER')+'</span></td></tr>').join('');
$('calcContent').innerHTML='<div class="sectionlabel">Geometry</div><div class="eq">Rise = (span / 2) tan(pitch) = '+fmt(d.v.width/2*Math.tan(d.v.pitch*Math.PI/180),3)+' m</div><div class="eq">Panels = '+d.v.panels+' · truss spacing = '+d.v.spacing+' m · tributary panel width = '+fmt(d.v.width/d.v.panels,3)+' m</div><div class="sectionlabel">Load mapping · representative common truss</div><div class="eq">Nodal load = q × tributary panel width × truss spacing</div><div class="eq">D = '+fmt(d.v.dead,3)+' kPa; Lr = '+fmt(d.v.rooflive,3)+' kPa; W uplift input = '+fmt(d.v.wind,3)+' kPa</div><div class="eq">Total service vertical effects per truss: D '+fmt(d.loadTotals.D/1000,2)+' kN · Lr '+fmt(d.loadTotals.Lr/1000,2)+' kN · W uplift '+fmt(d.loadTotals.W/1000,2)+' kN</div><div class="sectionlabel">Strength combinations screened</div>'+d.combos.map(c=>'<div class="eq">'+c.name+' → peak absolute axial force '+fmt(Math.max(...c.forces.map(Math.abs))/1000,2)+' kN</div>').join('')+'<div class="sectionlabel">Member resistance screening</div><div class="eq">Tension screen: φTn = 0.90 Fy Ag · Compression screen: φPn = 0.90 Fcr Ag, Fcr = 0.658^(Fy/Fe) Fy or 0.877 Fe; Fe = π²E/(KL/r)²</div><div class="eq">Trial section area = '+fmt(d.area)+' mm² · assumed r = '+fmt(d.v.r)+' mm · K = '+fmt(d.v.K,2)+' · Fy = '+fmt(d.v.fy)+' MPa</div><p class="explain">This uses gross yielding and an idealized column curve as screening only. It does not check net-section fracture, local slenderness, combined forces, connection strength, member bending, lateral bracing, or full code requirements. Reactions, displacements and all element forces are calculated by an elastic 2D truss stiffness model.</p>';
$('optContent').innerHTML='<p class="explain">The optimizer tests an illustrative set of uniform gross areas from '+catalog[0]+' to '+catalog.at(-1)+' mm², selects the first area passing this model\'s axial screening, then calculates a fit score from the selected area versus its smallest feasible catalog entry. It is a material-use heuristic, not a global lifecycle-cost optimizer.</p><div class="bars">'+d.grouped.map(g=>'<div class="barrow"><span>'+g.type+'</span><div class="bar"><i style="width:'+Math.min(100,g.util*100)+'%;background:'+(g.util<=1?'var(--teal)':'var(--red)')+'"></i></div><b>'+fmt(g.util*100,0)+'%</b></div>').join('')+'</div><div class="sectionlabel">Selected trial section</div><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Area '+fmt(d.area)+' mm²</span><span class="chip">Modeled truss steel '+fmt(d.massOne,0)+' kg</span><span class="chip">Roof-wide indicator '+fmt(d.totalMass/1000,2)+' t</span><span class="chip">Screening rating '+$('rating').textContent+'</span></div><p class="explain">For practical optimization, compare real section tables and member-by-member sizes, stock lengths, connection plates, purlins, bracing and fabrication waste. This demo applies one area to every modeled member.</p>';
}
const canvas=$('scene'),ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');
function draw(d){let rect=canvas.getBoundingClientRect(),scale=window.devicePixelRatio||1;canvas.width=rect.width*scale;canvas.height=rect.height*scale;ctx.setTransform(scale,0,0,scale,0,0);let w=rect.width,h=rect.height;ctx.clearRect(0,0,w,h);if(!d)return;
const L=d.v.length,W=d.v.width,rise=W/2*Math.tan(d.v.pitch*Math.PI/180),ca=Math.cos(state.rot),sa=Math.sin(state.rot),s=Math.min(w/(L+W)*.85,h/(rise+W*.6+2)*.85)*state.zoom,ox=w*.5,oy=h*.60;
function project(x,y,z){let X=(x-L/2)*ca-(z-W/2)*sa,Y=(x-L/2)*sa+(z-W/2)*ca;return[ox+X*s,oy-(y*.85-Y*.28)*s]}
const line=(a,b,color='#45616e',width=1,dash=[])=>{let p=project(...a),q=project(...b);ctx.beginPath();ctx.setLineDash(dash);ctx.moveTo(...p);ctx.lineTo(...q);ctx.strokeStyle=color;ctx.lineWidth=width;ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([])};
let eave=0;
let corners=[[0,0,0],[L,0,0],[L,0,W],[0,0,W]], ridgeA=[W/2,rise,W/2]; // define roof via hip endpoints
// roof surfaces break at end hip run; long ridge endpoints
let run=Math.min(L/2,W/2),rx1=run,rx2=L-run,ry=rise;
let ridge1=[rx1,ry,W/2],ridge2=[rx2,ry,W/2];
let roofEdges=[[corners[0],ridge1],[corners[1],ridge2],[corners[2],ridge2],[corners[3],ridge1],[ridge1,ridge2], [corners[0],corners[1]],[corners[1],corners[2]],[corners[2],corners[3]],[corners[3],corners[0]]];
roofEdges.forEach((e,i)=>line(e[0],e[1],i<5?'#56e0c2':'#334957',i<5?2:1));
let count=Math.max(3,Math.min(8,Math.ceil(L/d.v.spacing)));
for(let k=0;k<=count;k++){let x=L*k/count;if(x<rx1||x>rx2)continue;let tf=[[x,0,0],[x,0,W],[x,ry*(1-Math.abs(x-L/2)/(W/2)),W/2]];
// use roof height along length hip boundary for ridge plateau
let ty=(x>=rx1&&x<=rx2)?ry:ry*x/rx1;
tf=[[x,0,0],[x,0,W],[x,ty,W/2]];
line(tf[0],tf[2],'#426675',1);line(tf[1],tf[2],'#426675',1);
}
let tr=d.nodes.map(([x,y])=>project(L/2,y,x));
for(let m of d.mem){ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(...tr[m.a]);ctx.lineTo(...tr[m.b]);ctx.strokeStyle=m.type==='Top chord'?'#56e0c2':m.type==='Bottom chord'?'#71b8ff':'#52788b';ctx.lineWidth=m.type==='Web'?1:2;ctx.stroke();}
tr.forEach(p=>{ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(p[0],p[1],2.5,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fillStyle='#d6f4ef';ctx.fill()});
}
ids.forEach(id=>$(id).addEventListener('input',run));$('panels').addEventListener('change',run);window.addEventListener('resize',()=>state.last&&draw(state.last));
document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x===b));document.querySelectorAll('.tabpage').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x.id===b.dataset.page));});
$('rotate').onclick=()=>{state.rot+=.28;draw(state.last)};$('zoom').onclick=()=>{state.zoom=Math.min(1.8,state.zoom*1.13);draw(state.last)};$('fit').onclick=()=>{state.zoom=1;state.rot=.45;draw(state.last)};
$('reset').onclick=()=>{let defaults={length:12,width:8,pitch:25,spacing:1.2,panels:6,dead:.75,rooflive:.96,wind:.8,fy:250,E:200000,r:20,K:1};for(let k in defaults)$(k).value=defaults[k];state.zoom=1;state.rot=.45;run()};
$('export').onclick=()=>{if(!state.last)return;let d=state.last,txt='HIPSTEEL — PRELIMINARY STUDY ONLY\nNot for construction, permitting, or procurement. Engineer review required.\n\nGeometry: '+d.v.length+' x '+d.v.width+' m, pitch '+d.v.pitch+' deg, spacing '+d.v.spacing+' m\nLoads: D '+d.v.dead+' kPa, Lr '+d.v.rooflive+' kPa, assumed net uplift '+d.v.wind+' kPa\nUniform area: '+d.area+' mm2\nScreen status: '+(d.feasible?'PRELIMINARY PASS':'NOT SIZED')+'\nMaximum screening utilization: '+(d.util*100).toFixed(1)+'%\nEstimated roof steel indicator: '+(d.totalMass/1000).toFixed(2)+' t\nRating: '+$('rating').textContent+'\n\nSimplified 2D axial truss model; hip framing not analyzed. Confirm all loads and code checks independently.';let a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([txt],{type:'text/plain'}));a.download='hipsteel-preliminary-summary.txt';a.click();URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href)};
run();
})();
</script></body></html>
